        'This isn\'t a simple yes or no, and it deserves an honest answer rather than a tidy one. As a general population statistic, C-sections do carry higher rates of certain risks, infection, bleeding, blood clots, and longer recovery, than uncomplicated vaginal births. But when there\'s a genuine medical reason for a C-section, it becomes the lower-risk choice for that specific situation, not the higher-risk one. Both statements are true at once.',
