      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.whyMatters, '', [
        'A few myths worth clearing up directly, since they cause real, unnecessary guilt. "C-section is the easy way out": it\'s major abdominal surgery, with its own real pain, healing time, and recovery, not an easier path. "Vaginal birth is always the safer choice": this isn\'t universally true either; in situations like a breech baby or a low-lying placenta, attempting a vaginal birth can genuinely be riskier than a planned C-section. "A C-section means you\'ll bond less with your baby, or that it\'s a lesser birth": research doesn\'t support this; how you deliver isn\'t what determines your bond with your baby. On the actual numbers, population studies comparing "C-section vs vaginal birth" are measuring something slightly unfair to begin with; they mostly compare C-sections done for a medical reason against straightforward, low-risk vaginal births, which naturally makes the C-section group look riskier on paper, even though the comparison itself is uneven.',
