      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'As your baby moves lower, they take up less space directly under your ribs and diaphragm, which is exactly why breathing can genuinely feel easier once this happens. That same movement puts your baby\'s head closer to your bladder and pelvic floor, which is why increased pressure, more frequent urination, and a heavier, achier feeling low down often follow.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'For first-time mothers, lightening often happens two to four weeks before labour begins. If you\'ve given birth before, it may not happen until much closer to labour, sometimes not until labour itself. Either pattern is normal; timing varies considerably and doesn\'t predict exactly when labour will start.',
