    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'The mucus plug is a thick collection of mucus that seals your cervix during pregnancy, protecting your womb from bacteria. Losing it, sometimes called a "show," can be a sign labour is approaching, but it can happen anywhere from weeks before labour to right at its start.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'As your cervix begins to soften and change in preparation for labour, this thick plug can loosen and pass, sometimes all at once, sometimes gradually over a few days. It may look clear, pink, or slightly streaked with blood, which is completely normal and different from heavier bleeding.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Losing your mucus plug on its own isn\'t a reason to rush to the hospital; it\'s simply worth noting when it happened and watching for other signs like regular contractions or your waters breaking. Some women never notice losing it at all, which is equally normal.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
