      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.whyMatters, '', [
        'Your waters breaking, medically called rupture of membranes, means the fluid-filled sac around your baby has torn, and it can feel like a sudden gush or a slow, steady trickle. Both are normal ways for this to happen; a trickle doesn\'t mean it\'s any less real or urgent than a gush.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Once your waters break, labour often follows within hours, though timing varies. Note when it happened, whether the fluid was clear or had any colour or odour, since fluid that\'s greenish, brownish, or foul smelling is worth flagging specifically to your care team. If you\'re genuinely unsure whether it was your waters or urine leaking, that\'s common too; a simple test at the hospital can tell the difference.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
