    month: 8,
    question: 'Can anything I do naturally help start labour?',
    category: 'Labour & Birth Prep',
    applicability: 'Month 8 onward (weeks 36+)',
    canI: 'Do',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Honestly, the evidence is mixed and weaker than most lists online suggest. Walking has a small amount of supporting evidence. Dates, eaten daily in the last few weeks, have genuinely better evidence than most other suggestions, including some Indian-relevant research. Spicy food, sex, and most home remedies have little to no evidence behind them, and castor oil specifically carries real risks.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.whyMatters, '', [
        'A few myths worth clearing up directly. Spicy food is a popular belief with essentially no evidence behind it; at most, it may upset your stomach. Sex is genuinely uncertain, some theories suggest it might help, one study even suggested it might slightly reduce the chance, so the honest answer is "we don\'t really know." Castor oil is the one to actively avoid without your doctor\'s direct guidance, since it can cause significant digestive upset and, in some cases, has been linked to your baby passing stool before birth, which can cause complications. Dates stand out as the one option with more consistent research behind it. A few clinical trials, including work relevant to South Asian diets, found that eating around 70 to 75 grams of dates daily from 36 to 37 weeks was linked to better cervical readiness, shorter labour, and fewer inductions, though the studies are still relatively small.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Our honest take: dates are a reasonable, low-risk thing to try if you enjoy them, given the research behind them, though they shouldn\'t be treated as guaranteed to work for you specifically. Walking is worth doing anyway for your general wellbeing, whether or not it nudges labour along. Skip castor oil unless your doctor specifically directs you to use it.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Ask your doctor before trying any herbal remedy or supplement, and definitely before considering castor oil.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'A caution worth stating plainly: nothing here reliably overrides your body\'s own timeline. Most labour starts on its own schedule, not because of something eaten or done the day before.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'Evidence for most "natural induction" methods is genuinely weak.',
        'Dates have comparatively better research behind them than most alternatives.',
        'Walking has some supporting evidence and is worth doing regardless.',
        'Spicy food and sex have little to no reliable evidence either way.',
        'Avoid castor oil unless your doctor specifically directs you to use it.',
      ]),
    ],
