    canI: 'Do',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Aim to have your hospital bag ready by around 35 to 36 weeks, so you\'re not scrambling if labour starts early. Pack essentials for yourself, your baby, and your partner, along with your important documents, keeping in mind most Indian hospitals provide basics like diapers and maternity pads.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.whyMatters, '', [
        'Packing this early matters because labour doesn\'t always wait for your due date, and having everything ready removes one more thing to think about once things start moving. Many first-time parents overpack; hospital rooms are often tight on space, so a focused bag genuinely serves you better than a full one.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'For yourself, pack comfortable, loose clothing, a couple of nursing-friendly tops, toiletries, and any medication you take regularly. For your baby, a few soft outfits, a going-home outfit, and a swaddle or wrap are usually enough, since hospitals typically provide the rest. For your partner, a change of clothes and snacks go a long way. Don\'t forget documents: your identification, hospital registration and antenatal records, insurance details, and your birth plan if you\'ve made one.',
