    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'A birth plan is a short, written summary of your preferences for labour and delivery, things like who you\'d like present, your preference on pain relief, and any specific requests. It\'s genuinely worth making, even in a hospital setting where not everything can be guaranteed, since it opens a conversation with your doctor well before labour begins.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.whyMatters, '', [
        'A birth plan isn\'t a binding contract; it\'s a communication tool. Medical circumstances can and do change what\'s possible on the day, but having your preferences written down and discussed in advance means your care team already knows what matters to you, rather than learning it for the first time during labour.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Keep it short, one page is plenty, covering things like your preference on who\'s present, pain relief options you\'d like to try, and any specific wishes around your baby\'s first moments. Share it with your doctor at a visit in your third trimester, and pack a copy in your hospital bag.',
