        'Practising a simple pattern regularly in the weeks before labour, even just a few minutes a day, helps it become second nature, so you\'re not learning it for the first time mid-contraction. If you\'re exploring specific pranayama (a set of traditional yogic breathing practices) techniques, checking with a prenatal-trained instructor about which ones suit late pregnancy is worth doing, since not every practice is designed for this stage.',
