    question: 'What is a Non-Stress Test (NST), and why might I need one?',
    category: 'Scans & Appointments',
    applicability: 'Month 8 onward',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'A Non-Stress Test (NST) is a simple, painless test that checks how your baby\'s heart rate responds to their own movements, done using two soft belts with sensors around your belly. It\'s usually recommended in the third trimester if there\'s a specific reason to monitor your baby a little more closely, not as a routine test for every pregnancy.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.whyMatters, '', [
        'A healthy baby\'s heart rate typically speeds up when they move, and this test simply watches for that pattern over roughly 20 to 40 minutes. It\'s called "non-stress" because nothing is done to stimulate or stress your baby; the test just observes what\'s already happening naturally. Common reasons it\'s recommended include reduced movement, a pregnancy going past your due date, twins, or a condition like high blood pressure or gestational diabetes.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Eating beforehand and staying well hydrated can help ensure your baby is active during the test. A reactive result, your baby\'s heart rate rising as expected with movement, is reassuring and needs nothing further. A non-reactive result doesn\'t necessarily mean something is wrong; babies do have quiet periods, and your team will often simply try to wake your baby gently before considering further tests.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Ask your doctor why a Non-Stress Test is being recommended for you specifically, and what a non-reactive result would mean for your specific situation.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'This test essentially just watches your baby do what they already do naturally; it\'s less an intervention than a chance to check in.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'A Non-Stress Test (NST) checks your baby\'s heart rate response to movement.',
        'Usually recommended in the third trimester for a specific reason, not routinely.',
        'Common reasons include reduced movement, twins, or a condition like high blood pressure.',
        'A reactive result is reassuring; a non-reactive one doesn\'t automatically mean a problem.',
        'Eating beforehand can help ensure your baby is active during the test.',
      ]),
