  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-HEALTH-107',
    number: 336,
    month: 8,
    question: 'What does amniotic fluid actually do, and how much is normal?',
    category: 'Health & Medical',
    applicability: 'Month 8 onward',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Amniotic fluid is the fluid surrounding your baby inside the amniotic sac, cushioning them, allowing movement, helping their lungs and digestive system develop, and even helping regulate their temperature. A normal amount, measured by ultrasound as the Amniotic Fluid Index (AFI), typically falls between 8 and 18 centimetres, though the exact normal range shifts somewhat with your stage of pregnancy.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.whyMatters, '', [
        'This fluid does far more than cushion your baby; from around 20 weeks onward, it\'s mostly made up of your baby\'s own urine, swallowed and reprocessed in a continuous cycle that supports lung and digestive development. The volume naturally rises through most of pregnancy, peaking around week 33 to 34, before gradually declining a little as you approach your due date.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Your fluid level is typically checked at growth scans and Doppler scans from the third trimester onward, as one part of assessing your baby\'s wellbeing, not usually as a standalone concern. If a level outside the normal range is found, your doctor will explain what that specifically means for you, since both too little and too much have their own distinct causes and management, covered in their own FAQs.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Ask your doctor to explain your specific fluid level at any scan where it\'s mentioned, and what it means for your ongoing care.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'It\'s easy to overlook, but this fluid has quietly been your baby\'s entire world; cushioning every movement, tuning their lungs, all while looking, on a screen, like simply empty space.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'Amniotic fluid cushions your baby and supports lung and digestive development.',
        'From around 20 weeks, it\'s mostly made up of your baby\'s own urine.',
        'A normal Amniotic Fluid Index (AFI) typically falls between 8 and 18 centimetres.',
        'Fluid volume peaks around week 33 to 34, then gradually declines.',
        'Checked as part of routine growth and Doppler scans from the third trimester.',
      ]),
    ],
