  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-HEALTH-110',
    number: 339,
    month: 8,
    question: 'What is placenta previa, and what does it mean for my pregnancy?',
    category: 'Health & Medical',
    applicability: 'Month 8 onward (also relevant from mid-pregnancy scans)',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'Yes',
    held: true,
    heldNote: 'Yes, holds for Ishaan\'s sign-off (bleeding-adjacent condition, per Escalation Guardrail)',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Placenta previa means your placenta has attached low in your womb, partially or fully covering your cervix, the opening your baby would normally pass through during birth. It\'s classified into grades based on how much of the cervix is covered, and the grade largely determines what it means for your delivery.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.whyMatters, '', [
        'Doctors typically describe four grades: a low-lying placenta, where the edge is near but doesn\'t reach the cervix; marginal, where the edge just touches it; partial, covering part of the opening; and complete, covering it entirely. Many cases found earlier in pregnancy actually resolve on their own; the placenta doesn\'t move, but as your womb grows and stretches, the attachment point can effectively shift upward and away from the cervix, particularly if it was diagnosed with some distance still remaining.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'If this is found on a scan, your doctor will likely recommend a follow-up scan later in pregnancy to see whether the position has changed, since this genuinely happens often, especially with a low-lying or marginal placenta. Avoid strenuous activity and sex if you\'ve had any bleeding, and know that this diagnosis, especially found earlier in pregnancy, is far from a fixed outcome.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Ask your doctor which specific grade applies to you, and whether a follow-up scan is planned to reassess the position later in pregnancy.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        '"Placenta previa" can sound like a fixed diagnosis, but for many women it\'s actually a snapshot in time, one that often changes as pregnancy continues.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'Placenta previa means the placenta covers all or part of the cervix.',
        'Graded as low-lying, marginal, partial, or complete, based on how much is covered.',
        'Many cases found earlier in pregnancy resolve as the womb grows.',
