  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-HEALTH-114',
    number: 343,
    month: 8,
    question: 'What does the placenta actually do?',
    category: 'Health & Medical',
    applicability: 'All trimesters (foundational explainer)',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'The placenta is a temporary organ, grown specifically for this pregnancy, that acts as your baby\'s lifeline, bringing oxygen and nutrients from your blood while carrying away waste. It also produces hormones that support your pregnancy and helps protect your baby from many infections.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.whyMatters, '', [
        'Your blood and your baby\'s blood never actually mix; instead, the placenta works as a highly selective filter, passing oxygen and nutrients across in one direction and waste products back in the other, all through the umbilical cord connecting it to your baby. It also produces hormones like progesterone that maintain your pregnancy, and by the third trimester, it\'s a fully mature, remarkably efficient organ, having grown from nothing since implantation.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'The placenta\'s health and position are checked at various scans throughout pregnancy, since how well it\'s functioning directly affects your baby\'s growth and wellbeing. After your baby is born, the placenta is delivered too, sometimes called the "afterbirth," having finished the job it was built for.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Ask your doctor about your placenta\'s position or function if it\'s ever mentioned at a scan, so you understand what it means for you specifically.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'There\'s something genuinely remarkable about an organ that exists for exactly one job, grown from nothing, then given up entirely once that job is done.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'The placenta brings oxygen and nutrients to your baby and carries away waste.',
        'Your blood and your baby\'s blood never actually mix.',
