    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Choose a time when your baby tends to be active, lie down on your left side in a quiet space, and count each distinct movement, kicks, rolls, or flutters, until you reach 10, noting how long it took. This is a simple way to stay familiar with your baby\'s normal pattern, though it\'s worth knowing upfront that formal counting isn\'t required or done the same way by every guideline internationally.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.whyMatters, '', [
        'Lying on your left side is thought to genuinely improve blood flow to your placenta, which can make your baby a little more active during the count. Doing this around the same time each day, ideally after a meal, when babies tend to be more active, helps you build a real sense of what\'s normal specifically for your baby, which matters more than any generic number.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'There\'s no need to count formally every single day unless your doctor has specifically asked you to; simply staying generally aware of your baby\'s usual pattern is what most current guidance actually emphasises. If you do want to count, aim to feel at least 10 movements within about 2 hours; if you don\'t, that\'s the point to contact your doctor, covered in more detail in its own FAQ.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Ask your doctor whether they\'d like you to count formally, and how they\'d like you to let them know if you notice a change.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'The real goal here isn\'t hitting a specific number; it\'s simply knowing your own baby well enough to notice if something genuinely changes.',
      ], []),
